# W9 r5: the first prompt typed 14 s after launch, then `/trace`. fx warms one
# connection to the Gateway at launch and sends nothing on it (`warmAsync`,
# src/main.zig:706; `warm`, src/core/shared/http_pool.zig:76-102) and reuses a
# pooled connection idle for up to 30 s (`default_ttl_ms`, :14). The fake resets
# a connection that has sent no request for about 10 s, so fx's title call --
# the first request, on that connection, one attempt
# (session_title_generation.zig:168) -- fails before the fake sees it:
# `title` is missing from fx's gateway log and its `/trace` says
# `reason=transport_error detail=ReadFailed`. `titles.cap` is the same prompt
# typed 3 s after launch, where fx asks.
gateway titles-turns.json
titled titles-answer.json
seed titles-seed.json
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
wait 3
wait 14
type fix the renderer loop, it redraws every row twice
key Enter
wait 4
snap answered
title answered
type /trace
wait 0.5
key Enter
wait 2
snap trace
reports report
gwlog
